Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: sm8250: stop forcing S16_LE on the back ends

retroforge, 2026-11-09: description and the else-branch comment added,
code unchanged. The patch is named for compressed playback, which it
never handles.

89be3c15a58b ("ASoC: qcom: sm8250: explicitly set format in
sm8250_be_hw_params_fixup()") adds S16_LE to every back end's format
mask, which in practice runs the back ends at 16 bits. This keeps that
only when the link has compr_ops, but the fixup runs on back-end links
and nothing in sm8250.c or common.c sets compr_ops on them. The test is
never true, so this is an unconditional revert of 89be3c15a58b: every
back end keeps the format the front end negotiated, compressed or not.
---
diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
index 9039107972e2..91207bd41652 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/sm8250.c
@@ -44,7 +44,17 @@ static int sm8250_be_hw_params_fixup(struct snd_soc_pcm_runtime *rtd,
 
 	rate->min = rate->max = 48000;
 	channels->min = channels->max = 2;
-	snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);
+
+	/* Only force S16_LE format for compressed playback */
+	if (rtd->dai_link->compr_ops) {
+		/* This is a compressed stream, set format to S16_LE */
+		snd_mask_set_format(fmt, SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S16_LE);
+	} else {
+		/*
+		 * Back-end links never set compr_ops, so every stream lands
+		 * here: the back end keeps the front end's format.
+		 */
+	}
 
 	return 0;
 }
